Job description
We are seeking an Assistant Manager, reporting  to an Associate Director within the Hedge Division of Sanne, to develop and manage investor registers for funds administered by Sanne Group, as well as other investor registers for third-party funds. This includes being responsible for ensuring that all client relationships are managed in line with agreed service levels and that services and delivery is of the high standard expected by clients and Sanne Group. The incumbent must be detail-oriented with the ability to multi-task, prioritize work assignments, communicate effectively with internal staff and clients. Follow-through skills, supervisory and time management are critical elements of this position.
Key Responsibilities:
Identify the training and development needs of his/her team;
Mentor team members;
Ensure service levels are maintained;
Liaise with clients and assist with any queries from Fund Accounting, investors or fund managers;
Planning and controlling team workload and workflow;
Provide informal, on-the-job training for team members;
Liaise with other operational departments in respect of issues affecting the output of the Assistant Managers team;
Ensure that Investor Services procedures are correctly followed by the team under their supervision;
Ensure that all transactions are processed in a timely and accurate manner;
Demonstrate a good understanding of South Africa and Sanne AML requirements to ensure these are being adhered to with the support of compliance and senior management;
Support the team by liaising with Clients and Investors to collate the requisite KYC documents;
Review AML documents submitted by the team;
Review and provide process input into the tax year end reporting across Clients;
Ensure policies and procedures are followed and checklists completed in a timely manner;
Promote a risk management culture within the business by proactively highlighting areas where improvements can be made to reduce operation risk
Resolve client queries timeously;
Suggest and implement Investor Services procedures and process improvements;
Conduct mandatory performance appraisals on team members and ad-hoc reviews.
Review and test annual and bi-annual SARS reporting
Understand tax reporting within Hedge Funds.
Requirements
Skills / Experience Required:
The successful candidate must have:
BCom or related degree
In depth experience dealing with external parties such as fund managers, administrators, auditors and investors;
Proven Supervisory experience;
5+ years experience
Good knowledge of Investor Services processes;
Necessary management and interpersonal skills to manage a team of administrators;
Thorough knowledge of the different accounting methodologies used in the administration process;
A high level of attention to detail and accuracy in order to authorise transactions and check month-end statements and fund apportionments;
Ensure a high level of quality in the output of the Investor Services function;
A high level of problem-solving skills and
Exceptional communication skills.

Key responsibilities:
The successful candidate will be required to run and manage legal assignments in the legal areas referred to above.
In addition to the provision of sound legal services, these responsibilities will also include related marketing and administrative support including:
marketing and the preparation and submission of proposals;
the initiation and completion of the required KPMG risk procedures in respect of projects; and
invoicing and collection of fees for services rendered.
Skills and attributes required for the role:
Strong experience in the rendering of South African corporate and commercial law services as well as regulatory services;
Ability to provide innovative legal solutions to clients’ business and strategic needs;
Good skills to manage a team for successful delivery at the client;
Sound legal technical ability and knowledge of relevant South African legislation;
Strong ability to research legal questions and prepare sound legal opinions;
Good presentation skills;
Good command of the English language and effective drafting skills;
Ability to work under pressure and meet deadlines;
Client focused mindset and solution-orientated approach;
Excellent communication and interpersonal skills;
Ability to operate proactively;
Team player;
Drive and enthusiasm;
Commitment to excellence; and
Good IT proficiency in electronic research tools and MS Teams.
Minimum requirements to apply for the role (including qualifications and experience):
LLB at a South African University;
Admitted Attorney in South Africa;
approximately 5 to 7 years dedicated post articles experience in the legal areas referred to above.

About The Job
The CSIR has a vacancy for Procurement Specialist in the Supply Chain Management portfolio. The incumbents will establish and maintain procurement activities on a day to day operational and transactional level. The position is in Pretoria.
Key Responsibilities
Source goods and services, review and manage existing supplier relationship;.
Document and assess internal stakeholders’ business and sourcing objectives;
Collect macro- and micro-level market intelligence and analyze spend data;
Determine the total value of identified commodities and report accordingly to management;
Source suppliers that meet the CSIR procurement criteria and ensure compliance to the CSIR’s B-BBEE policy and programme;
Manage procurement transactional services ensuring reduction in purchase order cycle times and tracking supplier performance against targets;
Assess and implement automation of processes to improve service delivery;
Expedite orders to monitor quality, on time deliveries, preferential procurement and savings;
Ensure effective and timely response to user calls related to orders and deliveries;
Ensure the Procurement portfolio’s compliance with CSIR policies, procedures and IT standards focussing on standardisation of processes;
Keep abreast with business systems and new developments;
Manage procurement activities throughout the purchasing and supply chain;
Ensure that purchasing activities are provided in a fair, equitable, transparent, cost effective, efficient, and effective manner.
Build strategic, professional, and ethical relationships with internal clients and the CSIR suppliers.
Ensure buying activities support the CSIR’s supplier contracts and that the organisation’s strategic interests are considered in such relationships.
Create cost savings opportunities from bulk buying, proper contract management, pooling of efforts and economies of scale.
Accurate and timeous reporting of relevant management information.
Qualifications, Skills, And Experience
A Bachelor’s degree or equivalent three-year purchasing qualification with at least five years’ experience in procurement.
Good understanding of designated sector procurement.
Thorough working experience on construction related tenders.
Good understanding of the CIDB Act.
Good understanding and experience of Total Cost of Ownership (TCO).
Report writing skills.
Supplier evaluation experience and thorough understanding of business processes.
Sourcing, buying, negotiation, planning and organising skills.
Contract management skills and e-procurement knowledge.
High degree of accuracy, attention to detail and problem-solving ability.
Ability to meet demanding deadlines and good interpersonal skills; and
Excellent communication skills and strong customer service focus.
Closing Date:
13th, July 2022
