About the role
We are currently on the lookout for a talented Commercial Accounts Coordinator to work in our South Africa head office in Rosebank. This role will be reporting to the Area Business Manager.
The primary purpose of this critical role is to provide support for nominated customer accounts and support for the area business manager team to ensure the safe and efficient delivery of products and services to customers on multiple sites across the region.
A part of this role includes reporting on key metrics, providing analysis of commercial data, assisting Territory and Area Business Managers in preparing presentations & proposals to customers, supporting key administrative functions (such as Ariba, Letters of Offer, contracts, forecasting, etc.), leading specific process improvement initiatives
The successful candidate will also coordinate key commercial processes such as overtime & demurrage recovery, SOP forecasting, and the regional Business Improvement pipeline.
In return for your professional commitment, we can offer a healthy salary, genuine career pathways and support into leadership or engineering specialisation.
What you will be doing
Developing and maintaining key commercial information in the area. Provide support for customer relationship for nominated accounts and ensure all Rise and Falls are implemented;
Co-coordinating and monitoring of all forecasting within the region;
Regularly analysing key data, providing trend analysis and corrective actions;
Acting as SAP / system mentor for Area, ensuring effective use of systems, including direct training as required;
Identifying and developing account growth opportunities where appropriate;
Assisting with generation of Pronto’s, Resource Models and Letters of Offer;
Managing Debtor compliance on nominated key accounts;
Managing Customer Account Setup, Credit, Statutory, Master Data, CARMS, Supply Chain;
Regional coordinating, supporting, analysing and reporting including but not limited to:-
Monthly KPI reports
Sprint Team financials
Customer Reporting requirements
Assisting with development /update of customer Account Plans;
Demonstrated variation management to capture additional revenue streams;
Maintaining Operational Contract Summaries for Area;
Acting as Business Improvement Facilitator for Area.
What you will bring
Tertiary qualification in Finance or related;
3 -5 years similar experience;
Strong strategic and commercial acumen supported by sound commercial judgement;
Strong proficiency in systems such SAP, Excel, PowerPoint
Excellent data analysis & problem solving;
Ability to plan, influence & execute;
Effective communication abilities across all levels of the organisation;
Self-starter and demonstrated time management effectiveness.

What You Will Do
Leads, directs and develops the respective sales organisation in terms of its structure, people and performance to achieve maximum efficiency & effectiveness (including personal feedback & development);
Coach team members on sales techniques, procedures and standards that will help them achieve their sales targets;
Translate local business plans into sales plans, activities, and campaigns and manage the day-to-day activities of a sales team (in order to implement the organization’s overall sales strategy) for an assigned geography, channel, and/or customers;
Prepare sales forecasts and budgets; monitor sales volume, revenues, and costs against forecasts to identify problem/opportunities areas and adapt procedures;
Allocate resources according to up-to-date customer categorization to improve the overall performance of the sales team;
Negotiate sales with existing and new customers who are of strategic importance to the organization;
Contribute to the development of sales, customer retention, advertising, pricing, and distribution plans/strategies for area of responsibility
Responsible for customer profitability, generate knowledge on market development/customer needs and competitor activities and distribute to internal stakeholders.
Who You Are
Must have matric and tertiary qualification in Sales, Sales & Marketing or relevant Clinical field;
Minimum of 3 years successful Key Account Management / Sales Management experience in pharma/medical device industry;
Experience in blended selling, clinical sales and coaching for performance;
Have broad therapeutic knowledge of advanced and acute wound care as well as knowledge in vascular care and synthetic casting;
Excellent computer skills - Microsoft package experience is essential with CRM and Power BI knowledge;
Available to travel domestically extensively, and have valid RSA Driver’s License;
Adaptable to change, motivated and able to work independently to execute priorities;
Must be an excellent communicator (written, verbal and listening);
Excellent business acumen and engage in a professional manner with internal and external stakeholders;
Key relationships and knowledge of key stakeholders in the Hospital arena(Private & State);
Must be highly self-motivated and capable of leading a team and deliver stretched targets.
