The Junior Commercial Associate (JCA) role is positioned within the Commercial team of Mainstream South Africa. The key focus of the role is to support tender initiatives, specifically the REIPPP programme, financial close, and internal project tasks. The successful candidate will support both wind and solar submissions with the potential of Battery Energy Storage. Activities will cover aspects of financing, tender structuring, project management, supporting external stakeholder due diligence, financial models, stakeholder, and partner engagement. The JCA will be part of all of Mainstream’s bidding efforts into government tender opportunities, providing key supporting roles in the submission and financial close processes. The JCA will also provide ongoing support to the wider Commercial team as and when required.
What You Will Do?
Support the commercial team in REIPPPP bidding project tasks:
Financial close process
Internal project tasks
Core Responsibilities
Apply the proven Mainstream tender response process to REIPPPP bid submissions and thereafter financial close, through supporting the public tender team.
Collaborate with other Mainstream teams (development, energy analysis, procurement, engineering, grid, etc.) to execute tasks and streamline project work.
Develop your knowledge of the utility scale Renewable Energy bidding and financial close process through understanding of:
Provide market analysis on energy-related activities in South Africa and Africa.
Provide updates on regulatory changes in South Africa and Africa, with a focus on energy regulators, Government departments, utilities, the Carbon Tax Act, wheeling, energy banking, grid compliance requirements and any other energy related advancements in the region.
Support other Mainstream departments as it relates to commercial activities and outputs.
Other Responsibilities
Positioning the Mainstream brand as a recognised leading renewable energy player with stakeholders in existing and new markets.
Design and manage the project schedule, budget, and other project tasks for assigned projects.
Identifying and communicating on a timely basis all project barriers and risks, together with the strategies and approaches to overcome those barriers and risks.
Monitor SA and Africa market movements and news.
Work with the Development team to ensure that all required consents to invest, build and operate power plants are in place to reach financial close.
Coordinating with Procurement, Construction and Asset Management teams as applicable to ensure that procurement, engineering, energy analysis, construction and operations inputs are accurately reflected in bid responses.
Ensure that projects are developed in accordance with Mainstream’s SHEQ policies and procedures and in accordance with all applicable legislation. This includes adherence to and continuance of ISO accreditations: ISO 140001: 2015 and ISO 450001: 2018.
Lead project meetings and conference calls for assigned projects.
What We Require
Understanding of the renewable energy landscape in South Africa;
1-3 years work experience;
Minimum 3 year degree;
Self-starter and problem solver;
Motivated to succeed, be challenged and grow as an individual;
Collaborative team player;
Strong analytical and critical thinking skills;
Ability to take ownership and drive tasks as well as help create / modify existing strategy based on analytical learnings (thrive in an efficient work environment);
Organised, reliable, and deliver quality output;
Strong relationship building skills;
Strong MS Office skillset (Excel, PowerPoint and Word) a must;
South African citizen;
Mindset and ability to work / communicate in a fast-paced environment;
Fluent English language skills is a must;

Overview
The successful candidate will be exposed to a wide variety of Banking and Finance work, including opinion work and local and cross-border transactional work. If appointed, the candidate will develop excellent transaction management abilities as well as exceptional technical skills. The candidate will gain experience in debt transactions, preference share transactions and financial services law.
Key Responsibilities
Drafting of agreements and corporate documents;
Managing transactions (including cross-border transactions) and engaging with borrower and lender clients and local counsel in other jurisdictions;
Researching and advising on all aspects of South African financial services legislation and contract law (as it applies to finance transactions);
Attending independently to matters;
Assisting with the training of junior team members and clients, on request; and
Participating actively in the team's business development initiatives.
Skills, Abilities & Experience
The candidate should:
be admitted as an attorney and have at least three years post qualification experience in a Banking & Finance practice and be able to independently manage a transaction;
be achievement-oriented, focused and able to work under pressure in a deadline driven environment
have a thorough knowledge of the law applicable to South African debt finance transactions;
have strong analytical skills;
have the ability to self-regulate;
have excellent drafting skills;
have excellent communication skills (both verbal and written);
have a keen interest in financial services legislation;
be willing to read / keep up with market and regulatory developments applicable to finance law;
have the capacity for hard work, long hours and quick turnaround times;
demonstrate the ability to take part in and initiate client development activities;
demonstrate the ability to train junior team members; and
demonstrate the ability to manage client relations, billing processes and practice management in general.
This is a demanding but stimulating position which will require working outside of normal office hours, when necessary.

