About The Job
The CSIR has a vacancy for Senior Signal Analyst in the Radar and Electronic Warfare (REW) Impact Area within the Defence and Security Cluster. The incumbent will be responsible to perform research, development, knowledge application and technological innovation required for electronic support and electronic attack sensors operating in the microwave spectrum. The position is based in Pretoria.
Key Responsibilities
Work closely with the Research Group Leader to provide inputs to the innovation and technology strategies;
Mentor and coach engineers in various research and development projects;
Apply and integrate systems thinking concepts to solve real-world problems;
Research and develop innovative solutions within diverse knowledge domains, which could include domains such as Electronic Warfare (EW) Systems, Radar Systems, Radio-Frequency Systems, Antennas, Signal Processing, Algorithm Development, Software-Defined Radio, Statistical Analysis, Modelling and Simulation, etc.
Lead the development of advanced signal processing algorithms;
Analyse mathematical systems, their performance and induced system effects;
Simulate and analyse operation-based systems;
Simulate and undertake functional analysis of systems and subsystems;
Implement algorithms on systems;
Experiment with deployable systems to validate and improve algorithms;
Experiment with operational systems to characterise and understand performance;
Design and specify systems;
Develop prototypes using high level language (such as Matlab, Julia, Python and/or C++)
Liaise with and report to internal and external clients as well as stakeholders;
Analyse system requirements, capabilities, and functionality.
Qualifications, Skills And Experience
A Bachelor’s degree in electronic/computer engineering with at least five years’ experience in Electronic Warfare/Radar engineering environment in an analytical role.
A Master’s degree will be an advantage.
Post-graduate courses in the following will be an advantage:
Radar and/or Electronic Defence;
Signal processing;
Statistics;
Pattern recognition;
Sensor / data fusion.
Signal processing or system analysis experience will be an advantage.
Experience in Matlab, Julia, Python and/or C++. Proven experience in leading small and/or large project teams;
Proven experience and willingness in mentoring and coaching junior and senior staff members;
Proven experience and knowledge of EW product development project cycle: requirements, concept, design and development, testing, to market (client delivery);
Working experience in signal processing and analysis and/or system analysis;
Proven experience in client interfacing and relationship management.
Knowledge of the following will be an advantage: Antennas, Radio Frequency (RF) systems, Electromagnetic Theory and Propagation;
Knowledge of electronic hardware and software implementation;
Technical report writing and presentations skills;
Good communication skills (verbal and written).
Closing date:
10th, March 2022

Job Summary
To provide complex specialist advice and support in practice formulation and associated best practice improvement tactics; enabling the provision of specialist risk product expertise.
Job Description
Responsible for the design, development, configuration and testing of Operational Risk reporting and Dashboards. Enable end-user reporting and drive effectiveness of automation of reporting for the Group. Support the Head of Risk Enablement in driving the Reporting and Analytics strategy for Group Operational Risk.
Configure Cognos-hosted dashboards according to documented specifications;
Configure Cognos-hosted reports of low to medium complexity (detail or tabular summary) with or without infographic elements, according to documented specifications;
Configure Cognos-hosted reports of high complexity (profile or aggregate type which require integration between independent data tables) with or without infographic elements, according to documented specifications;
Provide substantial input into the technical soundness of documented specifications for dashboards and reports;
Provide input and assist on the design and maintenance, and participate in the testing of (ongoing) configuration of OpenPages and Cognos reporting packages;
Responsible for first-level functional and technical testing of own-developed/-configured reports and dashboards;
Assist with the analysis, enhancement, refinement, and maintenance of existing Cognos-hosted queries, dashboards and reports;
Facilitate the identification of data quality or configuration shortcomings / limitations, as it relates to the scoped and assigned reports and dashboards for development or enhancement;
Participate in facilitating ad-hoc user training on technical aspects pertaining to Cognos;
Perform peer review (quality assurance) on other Cognos-related developments / configurations;
Produce and present proof-of-concepts or simulated mock-ups of new or experimental reporting/dashboarding elements, where required;
Facilitate report and dashboard migration from older/outdated reporting packages;
Education
Bachelor`s Degrees and Advanced Diplomas: Business, Commerce and Management Studies (Required)
