About The Job
The CSIR has a vacancy for an Operations Manager in the Mining and Manufacturing Clusters within the Mining, Manufacturing and Defence and Security Division. The incumbent will be responsible for supporting Cluster level operations to enable the delivery and achievement of short-term operational goals and targets as well as enable efficient and effective day-to-day operations. S/He will ensure that operations are effectively managed to deliver in-line with the cluster’s strategy and business plan including, but not limited to, optimal revenue generation, productivity, project/contract risk management, resource loading, facilitating engagement with central portfolios including shared services. This position is based in Pretoria.
Key Responsibilities
Drive Cluster operations together with Cluster Executives, Impact Area and Research Centre Managers and relevant Project Managers;
Ensure the integration and streamlining of Cluster level business operations for effective and efficient delivery of value and impact to the relevant stakeholders;
Support Cluster executive with (and contribute to) coordinating the development of the annual Cluster business plans and budget across the impact area and Research Centres;
Implement and track the clusters’ strategy and progress against the business plan;
Support Cluster Managers to drive, monitor and coordinate the cluster’s Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) achievements across the impact areas to achieve business objectives;
Support Cluster Managers to co-ordinate quarterly compilation and submission of Cluster reports and KPIs (including supporting documentation and evidence);
Ensure CSIR Quality Management System implementation within the clusters;
Develop and implement systems, processes and solutions to improve the effectiveness and efficiency of the business operations of clusters;
Develop and implement systems to support Clusters’; Impact Areas and Research Centres to monitor and improve productivity;
Coordinate resources to support and enable the core of business operations including support functions in collaboration with Cluster Executives, Impact Area and Research Centre Managers and relevant Project Managers;
Contributes to the budgeting process in collaboration with Finance, line management as well as the Business Development and Commercialisation portfolio;
Ongoing support of Clusters to understand, monitor and manage critical drivers of cost appropriately;
Monitor Service Level Agreements (SLAs) with central portfolios;
Develop, improve and maintain business systems including quality;
Exchange information, track service delivery progress and quality, assist with service improvement efforts and report progress to Divisional Operations Manager and Cluster executives;
Monitor and manage risks including contracts and projects across the clusters;
Manage Parliamentary Grant (PG) allocation process to align with business development initiatives and monitor progress for the execution and delivery of revenue;
Manage PG administration (tracking of allocations, tracking progress, tracking Strategic Investment Management System (SIMS) registration, etc.);
Co-ordinate efforts across the Cluster to understand technology/offering/capability needs and identifying opportunities for cross Cluster collaboration
Implement the capability management guideline of the organisation within the clusters;
Monitor and optimise resource loading across the Clusters for project delivery and enhancing productivity;
Establish the risk management system (including Health and Safety) in the Cluster and works with relevant portfolios to support Cluster risk management.
Qualifications, Skills And Experience
An Honours degree in relevant science or engineering domain with at least five years’ experience in complex, multi-projects and matrix type environment with a solid track record in the following:
Operational planning and implementation.
Strategy development and tracking thereof.
Solid understanding of business planning and regulatory issues.
Project and programme management.
Project and portfolio management.
Business and finance management.
Business development experience.
Stakeholder relationship management experience.
Risk management.
A solid grasp of data analysis and performance metrics, for informed decision making.
A Post-graduate Business Administration qualification will be advantageous;
Relevant certification or accreditation in operations management will be advantageous
The incumbent should have
:
Organisational skills;
Excellent communication skills with strong business understanding – both verbal and written;
Ability to diagnose problems quickly and have foresight into potential issues;
Advance MS Office suite, including presentations.
PLEASE NOTE THAT FEEDBACK WILL BE GIVEN TO SHORTLISTED CANDIDATES ONLY.

About The Job
The CSIR has a vacancy for a Mechanical Engineer in the Industrial Robotics research group within the Centre for Robotics and Future Production, Manufacturing cluster. The incumbent will be responsible for designing, developing and integrating mechanical aspects of mechatronic projects where electronic, electrical and mechanical systems interact. This position is based in Pretoria.
Key Responsibilities
Develop mechanical designs for different projects;
Develop, design, build, test, and inspect mechanical devices and systems, such as machines, tools, and appliances;
Be part of project team that delivers results on brief on budget and on time;
Raise personal, team and institutional profiles through publishing original research and presenting work at national and international conferences and workshops;
Interact with peers within fields of expertise both within and outside the CSIR to generate new knowledge;
Supervise int erns and vacation students;
Stay abreast in field of expertise with respect to new approaches in tools, methods or technologies.
Key Qualifications, Skills And Experience
A Bachelor’s degree in mechanical or mechatronics engineering with at least three years of experience in mechanical or mechatronic design, development and integration;
During the above years of experience there should be evidence of experience in mechanical CAD (NX, SolidEdge, SolidWorks);
Knowledge of design techniques, tools, and principles involved in production of precision technical plans, blueprints, drawings, and models.
The incumbent must have hands-on workshop skills and NC Lathe/Mill experience;
Demonstrated skills in analytical thinking, flexibility and adaptability, planning and organising, problem solving, good verbal and written communication, research and report writing, teamwork, industry skills, self-management (planning, prioritising and time management – includes the ability to work independently), systems level thinking, multi-disciplinary knowledge.
Shortlisted candidates will be requested to provide a portfolio of work, to be discussed in Interviews.

Introduction
IBM Research Scientists are charting the future of Artificial Intelligence, creating breakthroughs in quantum computing, discovering how blockchain will reshape the enterprise, and much more. Join a team that is dedicated to applying science to some of today's most complex challenges, whether it’s discovering a new way for doctors to help patients, teaming with environmentalists to clean up our waterways or enabling retailers to personalize customer service.
Your Role and Responsibilities
IBM Research is one of the world’s largest and most influential corporate research labs, with an unmatched investment in research and core science, and a commitment to invent the future of technology by making scientific breakthroughs that will transform industry and society. We innovate and imagine the future and have a strong commitment to develop the next generation of top research talent. We host many scientists, visiting academics and students in the belief that it takes broad collaboration between the brightest minds to create innovations that make the world work better.
With the IBM Research Africa internship initiative, we are reaching out to outstanding young research talent in South Africa and invite qualified masters and doctoral students to apply for a 6 to 12-month internship position at the IBM Research lab in South Africa and take up this opportunity to work at a world-class research lab on some of the grand challenges and pressing problems that we are facing today. Candidates will gain insights into real industry challenges and obtain hands-on experience that should be valuable to their university and faculty. Candidates will bring back knowledge of IBM’s advanced technologies and contacts throughout IBM Research.
The ideal candidates should have an applied knowledge in some of the following fields: data science, cloud computing, artificial intelligence, Internet of things, computer vision, software engineering, applied physics and statistics. Successful candidates will develop and deploy proof of concept technologies and algorithms for the projects they are assigned to. The candidate will be expected to demonstrate the ability to define research questions, formulate hypothesis, and develop and demonstrate innovative solutions using cutting edge technologies. Furthermore, the candidate will be expected to collaborate extensively with internal and external teams.
Research projects will mostly be characterized by data driven innovation and machine learning, example research projects include: unsupervised machine learning on the cloud, traffic optimization, TB contact tracing, pulsar detection, genomics, computational biology, natural language processing applications in medicine, image analysis, air quality management, and stream processing analytics for the Square Kilometer Array radio astronomy project. Many of the research projects will be geared towards having transformational impact in South Africa and across the African continent.
The internship is open to any recognized MSc, MEng or PhD candidate working in the following areas at the time of application: Computational Biology; Computer Science; Data Science; Electrical, Electronic or Computer Engineering; Genomics; Industrial Engineering; Physics; Service Science; Statistics.
