Job Description
The Strategic Information Director (SID) will lead monitoring, data analysis, reporting, evaluation, and research interventions for the Activity and serve as senior technical specialist in data quality and data analytics. They will be responsible for data quality and accurate results reporting. The SID will be responsible for providing both written and visual data results that can be incorporated into programming and the communications strategy to support CSE within the Department of Basic Education system. The SID will lead efforts to strengthen monitoring and evaluation, and performance reporting within all the geographic areas of Activity, which may include overseeing support to provinces and districts to monitor, document and analyze the performance of their HIV services and activities and ensure data quality. The SID will analyze relevant data under the MER and custom indicators and provide analysis on performance trends. The SID will liaise with relevant technical advisers and counterparts responsible for district and provincial level strategic information and monitoring and evaluation and support coordination with national education management information systems. The SID will manage the Monitoring and Evaluation team.
Qualifications
Education:
Master’s degree (or foreign equivalent) in public health, health sciences, data analytics, or a similar relevant field.
Skills and Experience:
A minimum of 10 working on monitoring, evaluation and research in the HIV and AIDS, education, social welfare, and health fields;
Data analytics and monitoring and evaluation experience in health programs, education programs or other similar fields;
Demonstrated experience managing data and designing monitoring and evaluation methodologies, indicators, and tools, with progressively increasing responsibility;
Demonstrated expertise in the design and implementation of rigorous quantitative and qualitative research reviews, rapid appraisals, etc., and methods for data analysis;
Hands-on practical experience setting up and managing M&E systems for education and/or health programs in developing countries, and the ability to coach and train others in their use;
Demonstrated supervisory experience, interpersonal skills and team building experience;
Knowledge of the South African landscape including health, education and social development; and
Experience with USAID, specifically, PEPFAR-funded DREAMS programing is a benefit.
Experience in monitoring, evaluation and research within the South African school system is preferred.
Additional Information
Please Note: This position is not eligible for relocation or posting allowances and the salary will be paid in South African Rand.
All your information will be kept confidential according to EEO guidelines.
Applications are encouraged to be submitted via SmartRecruiters.
Due to the volume of applications submitted, only finalists will be notified. No phone calls, please.

About the job
Do you love analysing and interpreting data? Are you a performance driven individual and does it excite you that your insights can make worldwide changes? Then you may be the right fit for this position…
About Hepstar
Hepstar is a Cape Town based TravelTech company that focusses on the supply and optimisation of travel ancillary products and services for airlines, online travel agencies and travel technology companies, particularly products offered to customers during the online ticket booking process. We are passionate about building and maintaining our proprietary technology stack that facilitates our ability to increases ancillary attachment rates and revenue from the sale of travel ancillaries while ensuring customer needs are met and customer experience is personalised. Data driven decision-making forms part of our daily lives of solving product recommendation and merchandising challenges. Hepstar has been recognised for its pioneering software, not only in Africa but also across the world.
We are a team of individuals who are passionate, dynamic and hard working. We are here to challenge traditional business models and incite disruptive changes within the industry we operate in!
Purpose of the role
We are looking for a highly motivated individual who loves analysing data from multiple sources to deliver innovative analytical solutions to complex problems that directly impact the company's bottom-line.
Under the supervision of the Head of Data Science & Analytics, you will plan and execute data analysis projects to extract relevant insights from medium to large data sets. The data will be used to monitor client performance, identify client and company opportunities, measure product performance and can influence the company’s strategic roadmap.
Daily activities include, but are not limited to
Communicate actionable insights to internal and external audiences with pro-active recommendations using statistical techniques;
Create and maintain reporting templates and dashboards;
Manage data quality and manage processes to increase this;
Create automated tools which identify performance trends and business opportunities;
Identify and scope opportunities for process automation.
Qualification
Relevant qualification in statistics, computer science, research or similar.
Skills
Strong planning, organising and time management skills;
Strong analytical skills with the ability to independently collect, organise, analyse, and disseminate significant amounts of information with attention to detail and accuracy;
Creative mind to use data to solve business challenges;
Basic programming skills, particularly SQL, R and/or Python;
Advanced MS Office skills (especially MS Excel pivot tables);
Proficiency in available data analytics tools and experience in manipulating and analysing large data sets (e.g. SQL, R, Python, Matlab, KNIME, Pandas, Google Big Query, Google Data Studio, Microsoft Power BI);
Knowledge of and experience with data analytics tools and techniques (Predictive analytics experience/knowledge is a plus).
Competencies
Ability to independently drive projects with little direction;
Attention to detail;
Proactive;
Ability to clearly and effectively communicate his/her point of view;
Contributes to discussions of technical and non-technical nature;
Can translate technical jargon into plain language;
Collaborative team player with a win-win mindset;
Reaches out to peers and cooperates with supervisors to establish collaborative working relationship;
Regularly conducts cross-skilling and training with peers;
Ability to embrace change;
Adaptable to changing business and team needs;
Thinks out the box and fins solutions to technical problems in creative ways;
Self-starter with plenty of energy who is able to take initiative.
Experience
Minimal 2 year BI and statistical reporting experience;
Ability to translate data analysis insights into actions;
Proven ability to complete projects and ad-hoc requests timeously and in line with requirements;
Experience in running statistical tests.
Not required, but a plus:
Experience in building predictive models, machine-learning approaches, clustering and classification techniques;
Experience in the tech, travel and/or fintech industry.
What Hepstar offers you
Gain experience in the traveltech space;
Be part of an incredibly dynamic, passionate and energetic team;
Flexible working hours.

