Who are we?
Working Adventures is a recruitment company helping connect adventurous individuals with big brands around Europe. We help German, Dutch, French & Scandinavian speakers find jobs in exciting locations such as Barcelona, Lisbon, Athens & Dublin.
Our whole team is remote-based so you’ll be working with colleagues from across Europe and even further!
What you’ll be doing:
Manage the recruitment and selection process for all internal positions
Create engaging job descriptions and deploy recruitment strategies to attract quality team members
Handle all day-to-day HR administrative related tasks including contract renewals, system & regulation updates etc
Onboard new team members and ensure they have a smooth start to life at the company
Build and improve processes including evaluations, onboarding & training
Be a company culture ambassador by creating engagement among the team, organise team events and create incentives
Requirements
You speak English to a fluent/native level;
You have 3+ years in HR & Recruitment;
Self Employed (or willing to register as);
Ideally, experience working from home or on a remote basis;
Have strong administrative and organizational skills;
Have experience in helping to build a company culture;
Fast computer and quick internet needed!
You’re a great multi-tasker;
You take initiative and you are very positive;
You have a spare room, office or quiet and calm area to work from.
What do you get?
Salary of €15 per hour gross;
A long-term freelancer contract with monthly invoicing (it’s your responsibility to be registered as self-employed and to pay your income taxes);
Part-time working hours of 20 per week;
Friendly co-workers from across Europe;
Great opportunity to make a big impact in a growing company;
A lot of responsibilities and working closely with the owners & manager.
Contract conditions
We would also like to inform you what the contract roughly will contain, so you have a better understanding of the working conditions:
Starting Date:
We are looking for someone who can start asap.
Contract:
You will receive a trial contract of 3 months for 20 hours per week. After successful completion of the trial contract, you’ll be offered a contract of 6 months with a 1 month notice period. We are looking for a long-term partnership, therefore, the length of contracts will increase in the future.
Salary:
As of your start date, your base salary will be hourly €15.00;
Tax & Employment Status:
You’ll be hired on a freelance contract and will not be a direct employee of Working Adventures. The amount you’ll be paid will be the total gross earnings and it is your responsibility to register in the correct form (self employed, registered company, etc) and to pay your taxes in the correct country. We’ll request proof that you are registered as a company/self employed. This is something Working Adventures cannot advise on. At the end of each month, you’ll be expected to invoice Working Adventures with the agreed-upon amount.
Sick leave:
For the 1st 3 months, If you can’t work due to illness, you’ll not get paid for that time. After this period, we offer additional vacations days to cover sick leave, doctors appointments etc
Paid Time Off:
Over the course of a year, you’ll receive 22 to 25 paid non-workdays (pro-rata);
National Holidays:
You’ll receive the national holidays of the country you live in;
Unpaid Leave:
As a remote worker, you are not entitled to unpaid leave;
Working Hours:
You’ll be expected to work 20 hours per week between the hours of 9am to 5.30pm (Dutch Time), Monday to Friday.

About the job:
The CSIR has a vacancy for an
Events Manager
in the Human Capital and Communications portfolio. The incumbent will be responsible for the planning and execution of CSIR events and stakeholder interactions in line with the CSIR brand, policies and client requirements. He/she will, in close collaboration with the External Communications Manager, proactively conceptualise events and oversee the implementation of events across the CSIR. This position is based in
Pretoria
.
Key responsibilities:
Provide strategic support and advice to the External Communication Manager on all events-related projects.
Conceptualise, plan and oversee the implementation of events in line with the event objectives, within an allocated budget and approved timeframes.
Provide strategic advice and input into the communication planning process as it relates to all events that are either hosted by the CSIR or in which the CSIR is participating.
Project manage events with an internal and external focus from conception to implementation and report back.
Produce periodic events reports, in line with organisational reporting.
Procure and arrange pre-event briefings with event suppliers and facility providers to ensure smooth execution of events.
Produce detailed proposals, event planning documents and cost breakdown as per event requirements for sign off and approval .
Liaise with colleagues to co-ordinate the creation, design and content development of event-specific marketing collateral and to fulfil event-specific editorial requirements
Implement protocol advice and etiquette at high level and during stakeholder visits
Compile post-event reports and provide content for the CSIR intraweb as and when required, and for internal and external events.
Manage relationships with suppliers, stakeholders, planning committees and other internal support structures to ensure quality and timely delivery of events.
Support the implementation of the CSIR’s Outreach and CSIR programmes
Manage and oversee the annual budget allocations.
Monitor and manage the co-ordination of logistics for the CSIR’s participation at strategic stakeholder events such as exhibitions and conferences.
Provide strategic advice and manage the execution of CSIR events, which may be in-person; hybrid; or virtual.
Manage event collateral requirements to ensure that appropriate CSIR promotional material is always available at events.
Supervise and manage events practitioners and general events assistants in execution of tasks assigned to them.
Manage portfolio’s task and project allocation as and when requested by the External Communication Manager.
Develop a CSIR events calendar, and manage its execution in collaboration with internal and external stakeholders.
Provide advice and support to the organisation’s administrative staff for events that are cluster/portfolio specific.
Manage the events storeroom, including furniture and inventory.
Monitor and update the CSIR’s events management framework, policy and guidelines documents.
Qualifications, skills and experience:
A Bachelor’s degree in Public Relations Management with at least seven years’ experience in events management, of which four years should be in project management;
Protocol Certificate;
Project management experience;
Advanced communication skills, both written and verbal;
Strong presentation skills and the ability to negotiate for a common goal;
Advanced computer literacy;
Creativity and innovation;
Adaptability (Ability to multi-task and handle pressure);
Networking skills;
Understanding of how to position/exhibit physical and non-physical elements through eventing, eg: technologies and capabilities;
Strong organisational skills;
Decisive and critical thinker;
Highly motivate individual who works well in large teams, yet self-directed;
Problem-solving skills;
Ability and confidence to engage with internal and external executives and senior leaders, including high-profiled stakeholders;
Well-versed in latest technologies and software for events as well as virtual eventing;
People management; and strong relationship building.
Closing date: 25 January 2022

