Communicate with empathy and adapt communication style to meet the needs of the situation and audience.
Anticipate the needs of others and take appropriate action.
Embrace different points of view and welcome opposing and conflicting ideas.
Uphold the firm's code of ethics and business conduct.
About the role
We are looking for a candidate to fulfil a dual role, performing administrative tasks as well as assisting with client deliverables on our audit engagements. If you are currently studying towards an accounting accreditation, this is the role for you.
Essential skills and experience
0 -1 years related experience gained in a professional environment
Proficient in use of MS Word (Advanced), Excel, Power Point and google office suite;
Pro-active and able to use own initiative;
Pay attention to detail;
Ability to interact with clients, managers and partners professionally;
Good writing and typing skills;
Good interpersonal and communication skills;
Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information;
Reliable, motivated, results-orientated, able to work under pressure, able to multi-task;
Team player;
