A National diploma in information technology, computer systems engineering or related fields with at least four years’ experience in system administration functions covering inter alia Microsoft Active directory, backups, environments;
A Bachelor’s degree or an Advanced diploma will be advantageous;
Experience in working together with multiple teams during the design, engineering, implementation and operations phases;
Experience with recovering IT Systems during a disaster recovery testing or real scenario;
Experience with implementing backup policies and schedules to ensure data retention strategies are met;
Experience in IT Systems audits;
Working experience in Data Centre Infrastructure e.g. Power Distribution Units (PDU’s), Racks, Cooling, Fire suppression, UPS’s, Generators and Physical security systems;
Working experience in management information systems (MIS) and reporting;
Working knowledge and experience with Access control & DVR monitoring and troubleshooting;
Working experience in design and implementation of processes and procedures;
Working experience in Service Management processes;
Working experience in the implementation, support, maintenance, and problem-solving on Virtualization technologies, Active Directory service technologies, Inventory management solutions, Open source and proprietary Operating Systems, WEB technologies, Collaboration, and e-mail technologies;
Elements of Project management experience, i.e. working within planned time constraints.
Specialist knowledge and experience of Microsoft Operating Systems;
Technical knowledge of the latest ICT System Operation disciplines and industry trends;
Working knowledge of Server Operating systems, Collaboration Systems, Integration of systems, endpoint client and other relevant ICT systems and discipline(s);
Knowledge and use of customer support management software;
