About the job
The Council for Scientific and Industrial Research (CSIR) is a leading scientific and technology research organisation that researches, develops, localises and diffuses technologies to accelerate socio-economic prosperity in South Africa. The organisation’s work contributes to industrial development and supports a capable state.
ICT Solutions Architect
About The Job
The CSIR has a vacancy for an
ICT Solutions Architect
in the e-Government Impact Area within the Next Generation Enterprises and Institutions Cluster. The incumbent will be responsible to design appropriate ICT solutions architectures based on client requirements; and leading the development and implementation of such solutions. This position is based in Pretoria.
For more info about the impact area or cluster, please visit https://www.csir.co.za/nextgen-enterprises-and-institutions.-systems
Key Responsibilities
Engage stakeholders and clients with a view towards translating their needs, business processes into appropriate ICT solutions and systems architectures;
Manage the overall concept and vision of the solution;
Conduct requirements analysis of the solution, as well as the realisation of the vision through research and software/system development;
Provide technical leadership to teams of engineers and software developers, throughout the research and development process;
Organise the development effort of a system or solution;
Develop high-level system or conceptual architecture;
Execute technology decisions in order to deliver the solution to the clients;
Qualifications, Skills And Experience
An Honours degree in informatics, computer science information technology or computer/ electronic engineering with at least ten years’ experience in software development and engineering, particularly in large, complex projects using modern web technologies (HTML5, Python, JavaScript, Angular/React/Backbone, node.js, Enterprise Java and/or Python);
Experience leading development using test-driven approaches and agile methods (e.g. SCRUM, SAFe)) is required;
Experience with the following would be advantageous:
Requirements and systems analysis;
Conceptual modelling;
Systems architecture and high-level design;
DevOps;
Test automation, continuous integration, continuous delivery;
Docker;
Kubernetes;
Other programming languages;
Enterprise Service Bus, Service-oriented architecture, Microservice architectures, Enterprise Messaging;
Data management and analysis, relational databases, SQL and related technologies, NoSQL databases;
Enterprise Service Bus, Service-oriented architecture, Enterprise Messaging;
Distributed version control and source code management (e.g. git);
Open source software systems and licences;
Product/service conceptualisation and manufacture; and
Planning for product support and maintenance.
Must have deep knowledge of the following:
Software engineering and development life cycle;
Solutions architecture and conceptualisation;
Systems architecture and integration;
Product development life cycle;
Excellent communication skills (verbal and written);
Technical and report writing skills;
Analytical and problem-solving skills;
Strong ability to think abstractly and conceptually and to see the big picture; and
Ability to think strategically.
Closing date: 29 October 2021
