About the job
About the job:
At Integrove we THINK BIG. We value innovation and allow our business and teams to grow through a journey of rethinking the art of the possible. Collaboration and knowledge sharing is encouraged, and we are continually developing our business and our people. Through positive attitudes, accountability, acting with honesty, integrity and respect, our fellow Integroovies, are a pretty “groovy” team to work with.
Integrove is looking for a
Data Modeller
to join our dynamic, fun, Integrove Family.
A day in the life of …. A Data Modeller:
Translate business requirements into conceptual, logical and physical data models optimized across different data domains and for various purposes. These solutions support information management, business intelligence, machine learning and data science.
Implement client requirements through new data strategies and designs across all data platforms (relational, dimensional, and NoSQL) and data tools (reporting, visualization, analytics, and machine learning);
Work with business and application/solution teams to implement data strategies, build data flows, and develop conceptual/logical/physical data models;
Identify the architecture, infrastructure, and interfaces to data sources, tools supporting automated data loads, security concerns, analytic models, and data visualization;
Analyse and profile the source data to understand data quality issues, relationships, patterns and rules in the data;
Work closely with business analysts, data architects, data administrators, database developers, and data scientists to design bespoke databases using a mixture of conceptual, physical, and logical data models;
Evaluating implemented data systems for variances, discrepancies, and efficiency;
Troubleshooting and optimizing data systems;
Assist with the design and implementation of clients data models based on business requirements;
Ensure data modelling deliverables are delivered according to project plan and budget to meet commitment to stakeholders; and
Ensure all data modelling activities and deliverables are aligned to the development methodology and to the data modelling principles and standards.
Requirements:
Tertiary Degree / Diploma (BSc Computer Science, B.IT or Informatics related degrees);
Microsoft Azure certified (would be an advantage);
3 + years of hands-on experience with physical and relational data modelling within relevant consulting or industry experience;
Experience with PowerBI functions;
Experience with data warehouse, data lake, and enterprise big data platforms in multi-data-center contexts; and
Experience in development of conceptual, logical, and physical data models.
Required skills and knowledge:
In-depth knowledge of data warehousing; Kimball;
Deep knowledge in big data platform design;
Data Management processes;
Excellent communication skills (explain technical concepts in MS Visio, MS PPT;
Expert knowledge of metadata management and data modelling tools;
Strong interpersonal skills; and
Advanced troubleshooting skills.
“If you have not been contacted by HR @ Integrove two weeks after application, please consider your application as not successful. Appointments will be made in alignment with Integrove’s Employment Equity plan. All the information submitted through the application process shall be used for the purpose of processing your application for employment at Integrove."

Description
Out There Media (OTM) is a leading global mobile advertising company that uniquely links mobile operators with advertisers via its proprietary, award-winning technology, Mobucks™. The company’s platform enables operators to become a substantial player in the digital ad space and unlock significant revenue streams for them, and brands and agencies to reach their audiences, in a highly targeted manner, leading to unprecedented levels of consumer engagement. OTM works with Fortune 500 companies such as Unilever, Pepsi, Nestle, L’Oreal, Coca Cola, P&G and mobile operators such as MTN Group, Vodacom, Vodafone, 9mobile, Starhub, Zain or Telenor. The Company is headquartered in Vienna, Austria with operations across the globe.
We are currently strengthening our team in Johannesburg and are looking for an enthusiastic, driven, motivated, dynamic and well-connected senior executive to undertake the role of
Managing Director (MD)
and lead our Sub-Saharan African (SSA) business. A strategist and a leader, you will be responsible for the overall success of the business by steering the company in the most profitable direction. You will be responsible for driving sales growth, managing the regional business, and working closely with OTM’s clients (mobile operator partners, and brands and agencies) to achieve OTM’s regional vision, mission, and long-term goals.
More specifically, the role includes both operational and commercial duties:
Full financial P&L responsibility and overall management of the SSA region with quarterly reports to the Chairman of OTM Africa on regional performance, financial budgets, business goals and strategic planning;
Responsible for the sales and account management function of OTM SSA. Drive new business development opportunities, while nurturing and growing the network of contacts within the industry to generate business leads. Build and foster relationships with the key stakeholders within the mobile advertising ecosystem such as brands, agencies, mobile network operators or publishers. Identify client needs and ensure profitable solution-based selling to increase revenue and create value added client relationships.
Effectively manage the relationships with all clients in the region and mitigate risks to the company; become involved in resolution of any issues at a country or regional level that may have an adverse effect on downtime or client relationships, while at all times ensuring compliance with local laws and regulations, as well as OTM policies and procedures;
Recruit, select and develop a well-motivated and skilled team capable of meeting the strategic demands of the business and market to ensure long term profitability. Manage performances of staff by motivating, training, coaching, and mentoring. Create a culture for success and performance;
Monitor the market developments and implement operational enhancements to improve market competitiveness by establishing and maintaining service differentiation in a competitive environment;
Requirements
University Degree(s) in related disciplines (e.g. Marketing and Sales, Media Management, Communication, Advertising, Business Administration, Economic Studies, etc.);
Proven experience in the advertising and media industry, in a senior leadership role, working within advertising agencies or digital media companies, or mobile operators, and being involved with digital strategy, managing digital advertising projects, digital transformation projects, programmatic advertising, etc;
Strong ties with media agencies or mobile operators in the region is a prerequisite;
The role requires:
Clear orientation to drive sales growth by working closely with brands and agencies, mobile operators and other partners;
Solid negotiating and closing skills;
Creative and innovative mindset, able to build commercial growth plans, strategize and drive business development activities that lead to growth;
Structured thinking and organizational mindset. Able to anticipate client needs, foresee potential obstacles and act upon them on-time;
Exceptional written and verbal communication skills. Ability to motivate and successfully lead teams through tight timeframes and simultaneously manage several projects;
Excellent in English - Ability to travel
Benefits
A competitive salary and bonus structure
Exposure to global network footprint
Become part of a vibrant and international team, while at the same time working with cutting edge technologies

